@ 17.8.4 - Proto-Indo-European to Coan Greek
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Tucker, R. Whitney (1969), “Chronology of Greek Sound Changes”. The American Journal of Philology 90(1):36 – 47; and Wikipedia contributors (2013), “Ancient Greek dialects”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. NB: This assumes that the adjective “Coan” refers to the “Ceos” Tucker mentions in the source.
	{[+laryngeal],m̩,n̩} > a
	{ bʱ, dʱ, ɡʱ } > { pʰ, tʰ, kʰ }
	s > h / #_
	s > h / V_V
	t > t͡s / _i
	j > h
